The struct `FungibleStakedSui { id: UID, pool_id: ID, value: u64 }` — the code's only write to `self` is `self.value`. `self.pool_id` is read (in the `EWrongPool` assert) but **never written**. So the code provably preserves `pool_id`.

The spec has **zero** `ensures` clauses — only two abort `asserts`. The sibling `split_staked_sui_spec` in the same file is the model of completeness (captures `old_pool_id`, ensures `pool_id(stake) == old_pool_id` plus the value change). The getter `fungible_staked_sui_pool_id_spec` exists with `no_opaque`, so the frame ensures is directly expressible.

